{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the man did as Joseph said.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: this is Menashe. And it is difficult, for Rashi in tractate Avot derives the age of thirteen for mitzvot from Shimon and Levi, for when they came upon Shechem they were only thirteen years old, when you calculate their years, and it is written of them איש חרבו על ירכו, and when you calculate the years of Menashe you will find that he was no more than nine years old at most, for he was born before the year of famine began, and even if you say he was born at the beginning of the seven years of plenty, even so he was only nine years old — seven of plenty and two of famine — and even so Scripture calls him איש. From the Rabbi Chaim, who said it in the name of the Rabbi Eliezer Avi HaEzri, and it requires investigation."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {0 "The phrase 'איש חרבו על ירכו' (each man his sword upon his thigh) is from Genesis 34:25, referring to Shimon and Levi at Shechem. The difficulty is that the same word איש is applied to Menashe, who was only about nine."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:02.624004773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}